    {
      "fragment_id": "PTX-9.3-CNOT-010",
      "document_id": "ptx-isa-9.3-html",
      "section_number": "5.2.2",
      "section_heading": "Restricted Use of Sub-Word Sizes",
      "html_anchor": "restricted-use-of-sub-word-sizes",
      "html_line_start": 3070,
      "html_line_end": 3076,
      "exact_quote": "The .u8, .s8, and .b8 instruction types are restricted to ld, st, add, sub, min, max, neg and cvt instructions. The .f16 floating-point type is allowed in half precision floating point instructions and texture fetch instructions. The .f16x2 floating point type is allowed only in half precision floating point arithmetic instructions and texture fetch instructions.",
      "context_before": "3069: </p>",
      "context_after": "3079: <p class=\"rubric\">Semantics</p>",
      "local_source_path": "documents/sources/nvidia/ptx/9.3/raw/ptx_isa_9.3.html",
      "source_sha256": "e2095c4ae00fe81fa18325b8e26c4a41b94965295c7affd7ff7f787fd98a8856"
    },
    {
      "fragment_id": "PTX-9.3-CNOT-011",
      "document_id": "ptx-isa-9.3-html",
      "section_number": "5.2.1",
      "section_heading": "Fundamental Types",
      "html_anchor": "fundamental-types-fundamental-type-specifiers",
      "html_line_start": 3053,
      "html_line_end": 3054,
      "exact_quote": "Bits (untyped): .b8, .b16, .b32, .b64, .b128",
      "context_before": "3050: row Floating-point",
      "context_after": "3055: row Predicate",
      "local_source_path": "documents/sources/nvidia/ptx/9.3/raw/ptx_isa_9.3.html",
      "source_sha256": "e2095c4ae00fe81fa18325b8e26c4a41b94965295c7affd7ff7f787fd98a8856"
    },
    {
      "fragment_id": "PTX-9.3-CNOT-012",
      "document_id": "ptx-isa-9.3-html",
      "section_number": "5.2.1",
      "section_heading": "Fundamental Types",
      "html_anchor": "fundamental-types",
      "html_line_start": 3062,
      "html_line_end": 3066,
      "exact_quote": "Most instructions have one or more type specifiers, needed to fully specify instruction behavior. Operand types and sizes are checked against instruction types for compatibility.\nTwo fundamental types are compatible if they have the same basic type and are the same size. Signed and unsigned integer types are compatible if they have the same size. The bit-size type is compatible with any fundamental type having the same size.",
      "context_before": "3061: end of Table 8",
      "context_after": "3067: In principle, all variables (aside from predicates) could be declared using only bit-size types",
      "local_source_path": "documents/sources/nvidia/ptx/9.3/raw/ptx_isa_9.3.html",
      "source_sha256": "e2095c4ae00fe81fa18325b8e26c4a41b94965295c7affd7ff7f787fd98a8856"
    },
    {
      "fragment_id": "PTX-9.3-CNOT-013",
      "document_id": "ptx-isa-9.3-html",
      "section_number": "5.2.1",
      "section_heading": "Fundamental Types",
      "html_anchor": "fundamental-types",
      "html_line_start": 3020,
      "html_line_end": 3022,
      "exact_quote": "In PTX, the fundamental types reflect the native data types supported by the target architectures. A fundamental type specifies both a basic type and a size. Register variables are always of a fundamental type, and instructions operate on these types.",
      "context_before": "3019:  in PTX, the fundamental types reflect the native data types",
      "context_after": "3023: Table 8 lists the fundamental type specifiers for each basic type",
      "local_source_path": "documents/sources/nvidia/ptx/9.3/raw/ptx_isa_9.3.html",
      "source_sha256": "e2095c4ae00fe81fa18325b8e26c4a41b94965295c7affd7ff7f787fd98a8856"
    },
    {
      "fragment_id": "PTX-9.3-CNOT-014",
      "document_id": "ptx-isa-9.3-html",
      "section_number": "5.1.1",
      "section_heading": "Register State Space",
      "html_anchor": "register-state-space",
      "html_line_start": 2613,
      "html_line_end": 2624,
      "exact_quote": "Registers (.reg state space) are fast storage locations. The number of registers is limited, and\nwill vary from platform to platform. The most common use of 8-bit registers is with ld, st, and cvt instructions, or as elements of vector tuples.",
      "context_before": "2612: </h3>",
      "context_after": "2625: Registers differ from the other state spaces in that they are not fully addressable",
      "local_source_path": "documents/sources/nvidia/ptx/9.3/raw/ptx_isa_9.3.html",
      "source_sha256": "e2095c4ae00fe81fa18325b8e26c4a41b94965295c7affd7ff7f787fd98a8856"
    },
    {
      "fragment_id": "PTX-9.3-CNOT-015",
      "document_id": "ptx-isa-9.3-html",
      "section_number": "9.3",
      "section_heading": "Predicated Execution",
      "html_anchor": "predicated-execution",
      "html_line_start": 7547,
      "html_line_end": 7550,
      "exact_quote": "All instructions have an optional guard predicate which controls conditional execution of the instruction. The syntax to specify conditional execution is to prefix an instruction with @{!}p, where p is a predicate variable, optionally negated. Instructions without a guard predicate are executed unconditionally.",
      "context_before": "7543: .reg .pred p, q, r;",
      "context_after": "7551: Predicates are most commonly set as the result of a comparison performed by the setp instruction.",
      "local_source_path": "documents/sources/nvidia/ptx/9.3/raw/ptx_isa_9.3.html",
      "source_sha256": "e2095c4ae00fe81fa18325b8e26c4a41b94965295c7affd7ff7f787fd98a8856"
    },
    {
      "fragment_id": "PTX-9.3-CNOT-016",
      "document_id": "ptx-isa-9.3-html",
      "section_number": "9.7.13.2",
      "section_heading": "Control Flow Instructions: @",
      "html_anchor": "control-flow-instructions-at",
      "html_line_start": 21826,
      "html_line_end": 21842,
      "exact_quote": "9.7.13.2. Control Flow Instructions: @\n@{!}p    instruction;\nExecute an instruction or instruction block for threads that have the guard predicate True. Threads with a False guard predicate do nothing.\n\nIf {!}p then instruction",
      "context_before": "21824: </section>",
      "context_after": "21843: <p class=\"rubric\">Semantics</p>",
      "local_source_path": "documents/sources/nvidia/ptx/9.3/raw/ptx_isa_9.3.html",
      "source_sha256": "e2095c4ae00fe81fa18325b8e26c4a41b94965295c7affd7ff7f787fd98a8856"
    }
